---
presentation: slidedeck
format: desktop
title: Demo Messages
subtitle: Gemini voice narration demo
author: Exergy LLC
lang: en-US
themes: [dark]
narrative:
  provider: gemini
  model: gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts
  voice: male
  pause_seconds: 3
  direction:
    profile: >-
      For Speaker 1: A warm, reflective male campaign-film narrator. Keep the
      delivery original; do not imitate any specific person's voice.
    scene: >-
      A sparse recording studio. The words accompany a black-and-white montage
      celebrating people who challenge convention.
    style: Intimate, assured, idealistic, and cinematic without sounding theatrical.
    accent: Native pronunciation for the selected language.
    pacing: Deliberate, with clean pauses between short sentences.
    notes: Let each final phrase land before the audio ends.
---
@id non-conformists
@layout cover

# Here’s to the crazy ones.

The misfits. The rebels. The troublemakers.  
The round pegs in the square holes.  
The ones who see things differently.

@narrative
  direction:
    notes: Begin as a quiet toast, then add warmth and conviction with each phrase.
  entries:
    - en-US: >-
        Here’s to the crazy ones. The misfits. The rebels. The troublemakers.
        The round pegs in the square holes. The ones who see things differently.
    - fr-FR: >-
        Hommage aux fous. Aux marginaux. Aux rebelles. Aux fauteurs de troubles.
        Aux chevilles rondes dans les trous carrés. À ceux qui voient les choses
        différemment.
    - es-ES: >-
        Esto es para los locos. Los inadaptados. Los rebeldes. Los alborotadores.
        Las clavijas redondas en los agujeros cuadrados. Los que ven las cosas de
        forma diferente.
    - de-DE: >-
        Ein Hoch auf die Verrückten. Die Außenseiter. Die Rebellen. Die Unruhestifter.
        Die runden Stifte in den eckigen Löchern. Diejenigen, die die Dinge anders sehen.
    - nl-NL: >-
        Een ode aan de dwazen. De buitenbeentjes. De rebellen. De onruststokers.
        De ronde pinnen in de vierkante gaten. Degenen die de dingen anders zien.

---
@id dcp-boring
@layout cover

# J:

I think DCP is kind of boring.

(sent handsfree from my second Tesla)

@narrative
  direction:
    style: Casual and offhand, like a voice text from a car.
    pacing: Natural conversational cadence; treat the parenthetical as a quiet send-status, not a punchline shout.
    notes: Keep “J” as a brief speaker tag, then the complaint, then the Tesla footer as an afterthought. Speak only the language of this script — never switch languages.
  entries:
    - en-US: >-
        J: I think DCP is kind of boring.
        Sent handsfree from my second Tesla.
    - fr-CA: >-
        J : Je trouve que le DCP est un peu plate.
        Envoyé mains libres depuis ma deuxième Tesla.

---
@id from-target
@layout cover

# From Target:

Dan, you owe us 100 compute credits, not to mention the compounding damage caused by implying to our customers that we would be giving away anything for free!

@narrative
  direction:
    style: Formal, clipped, and faintly indignant — a corporate complaint, not a toast.
    pacing: Even and pointed; let the free-giveaway clause land without shouting.
    notes: Read “From Target” as a sender line, then address Dan by name.
  entries:
    - en-CA: >-
        From Target: Dan, you owe us 100 compute credits, not to mention the
        compounding damage caused by implying to our customers that we would be
        giving away anything for free!

---
@id desjardins-fridge
@layout cover

# From Desjardin’s fridge:

Dan, your son is running out of milk! Be sure to bring some when you’re done.

@narrative
  direction:
    style: Flat, robotic smart-appliance voice. Even pitch, little warmth, slight Canadian English.
    pacing: Measured and slightly mechanical; do not rush the milk warning.
    accent: Canadian English.
    notes: >-
      Read “From Desjardin’s fridge” as a device sender line, then the warning to Dan.
      Stay in Canadian English only. Sound like a household robot, not a film narrator.
  entries:
    - en-CA: >-
        From Desjardin’s fridge. Dan, your son is running out of milk.
        Be sure to bring some when you’re done. Concentrated, not distributed this time - please

